{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791803541,"nonce":"cwGnQa9Foe7qktX3B1P5tMQiCgk=","title":"GADT cases do not refine sibling values or nested evaluator operands","message":"At the verified v58 checkpoint (1083/1092 on both hosts), TestGADT has 11 failed checks. The separate module-constructor patch removes the three result-type failures but leaves eight checks failing in a focused run.\n\nThe arithmetic probe uses Constant\u003cT\u003e, Binop\u003cS,T\u003e with OpAdd:Binop\u003cFloat,Float\u003e and OpEq:Binop\u003cS,Bool\u003e, and Expr\u003cT\u003e. In evalBinop\u003cT,C\u003e, matching OpAdd must refine C and T to Float in that case. The current MIR adds erased i64 bit patterns instead of emitting floating addition. RAYZOR_DUMP_MONO also shows evalBinop\u003cT,C\u003e calls missing explicit arguments and C remaining unbound. A return-only specialization leaves the operand parameter unknown; treating it as the result parameter gives incorrect equality.\n\nTestGADT.testFieldMatches also requires each TInst/TEnum case to independently refine sibling t.args (or tuple captures) through MyTypeKind\u003cT\u003e to String/Int, then restore the generic type outside the case. All six type assertions remain wrong despite their runtime reads passing.\n\nDo not substitute one global type for T across all cases or infer the existential operand parameter from the evaluator result type: OpEq returns Bool while its operands can be Float or String. Validate floating addition, unequal and equal floating operands, independent case types, and no leakage after each case.\n\nEvidence: target/conformance-checkpoint/gadt-evaluation-probe/GadtEvaluation.hx (native Haxe passes, v58 fails eval value), gadt-evaluation-v58-trace.log (pre/post monomorphization MIR), gadt-evaluation-v59a-mono.log, gadt-full-v59a.log.","files":null}]}